<title>SPAIN: Spain's BBV posts 24.8 percent rise in Q1 profit. [CORRECTED 10:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>Spain's BBV posts 24.8 percent rise in Q1 profit. [CORRECTED 10:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Bilbao Vizcaya group three months to March 31, (in billions of pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		24.73   vs   19.82</p>
<p> Net interest income		   123.65   vs   99.69</p>
<p> Ordinary margin			 185.69   vs  138.82</p>
<p> Operating margin			 76.84   vs   54.41</p>
<p> Fees and commissions		    42.95  vs     31.78</p>
<p> Financial/trading income		19.10  vs	7.35</p>
<p> Personnel costs			   67.34  vs     53.12</p>
<p> Depreciation				 9.65  vs	7.19</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    57.77  vs     42.61</p>
<p>(Corrects pre-tax profit from 51.58 vs 38.21)</p>
<p> Tax					   22.95  vs     16.35</p>
<p>(Corrects tax from 16.76 vs 11.95)</p>
<p> Net profit				  34.82  vs     26.26</p>
<p> Minorities				  10.09  vs	6.45</p>
<p> Net extraordinary losses		14.36  vs	2.87</p>
<p> Bad debt provision			13.90  vs     12.55</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
